{"title":"Incentives matter, installment #1637","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/925614173/0/marginalrevolution~Incentives-matter-installment.html","date":1759302340000,"content":"<blockquote><p>In the first three months of 2025, U.S. companies canceled, downsized or mothballed nearly $8 billion worth of supply chain projects — including more than $2.2 billion tied to battery plants. That single quarter exceeded the combined losses of the previous two years, according to Atlas Public Policy.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/ModeledBehavior/status/1973126565191098496\" target=\"_blank\">Via Adam Ozimek</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/10/incentives-matter-installment-1637.html\">Incentives matter, installment #1637</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/925614173/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/925614173/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/925614173/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/925614173/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/925614173/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/20/925614173/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/rss20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/10/inc